<title>UK: BOE revises money market shortage, no ops invited.</title>
<headline>BOE revises money market shortage, no ops invited.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England revised the money market shortage to 750 million stg from 850 million stg and said the residual shortage was nil following operations earlier in the day.</p>
<p>The Bank provided a total of 750 million stg assistance during the day and therefore did not invite operations at the afternoon round.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
